    "icxc_key": "oc.m8.d1_gr_GR_cog|ocVE.Apolytikion.text",
    "text_gr": "Ἐξ ὕψους κατῆλθες ὁ Εὔσπλαγχνος, ταφὴν κατεδέξω τριήμερον, ἵνα ἡμᾶς ἐλευθερώσῃς τῶν παθῶν. Ἡ ζωὴ καὶ ἡ ἀνάστασις ἡμῶν, Κύριε δόξα σοι.",
    "text_en": "You descended from on high, O compassionate One, and consented to a three-day burial, to free us from the passions. O Lord, our life and resurrection, glory to You!",
    "translations_en": {
      "Ages": "You descended from on high, O compassionate One, and condescended to be buried for three days, so that from the passions You might set us free. Our life and resurrection, O Lord, glory be to You.",
      "GOASD": "You descended from on high, O compassionate One, and consented to a three-day burial, to free us from the passions. O Lord, our life and resurrection, glory to You!",
      "Lash": "You came down from on high, O Compassionate, you accepted burial for three days, that you might free us from the passions. Our Life and Resurrection, Lord, glory to you.",
      "Repass": "From on high you descended, O compassionate one. You accepted the three-day burial to free us from the passions. O Lord, our life and Resurrection, glory to you."
    },
    "version_en": "GOASD",
